#AUTO 44
#NEEDED 0
# Crypto accelerator recon (issue 110n) — gather once, then de-select.
#
# The crypto block (0xFE380000) has no dedicated version/ID register on this
# part, so this is a presence/clocking check: ungate the crypto clocks and
# release their resets (a read while gated HANGS the bus), then read the first
# control register. A non-hanging read is the whole result — it confirms the
# block is reachable and clocked, for later crypto/identity work.
#
# Base, clock/reset bits, and the CLK_CTL read target are all confirmed against
# the TRM (Part1 Table 1-1 + Ch2, Part2 Ch4); see the note in
# src/019-probe-engine.c (crypto_probe). CRU writes done in C behind a CALL.

CALL crypto_probe
